      },
      "authorType": "TOPIC",
      "competitionRanking": 840,
      "content": "<p>I would like to bring the community's attention to a deceptive practice currently happening in the notebooks section to farm upvotes.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/atahalam/nvidianemotron-0-81-new-making-0-85-public-soon\" target=\"_blank\">nvidianemotron 0.81 new making 0.85 public soon</a></p>\n<p><strong>Why this notebook is fake and deceptive:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Output Copying (Plagiarism):</strong> The code inside this notebook is completely fake and does not generate the score it claims through actual modeling. Instead, it simply copies the <code>submission.zip</code> or outputs from other hard-working Kagglers' top-performing public notebooks directly into <code>/kaggle/working/</code>. </li>\n<li><strong>Clickbait Titles:</strong> The author intentionally uses misleading titles like <em>\"making 0.85 public soon\"</em> to deceive users and farm upvotes. Furthermore, they have a history of writing fabricated scores in the titles that are completely different from what the actual code inside achieves.</li>\n<li><strong>Disabled Comments:</strong> To prevent anyone from pointing out these issues or warning others, the author has deliberately disabled the comments section on the notebook.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>This behavior disrespects the hard work of original authors and clutters the platform with spam.</strong></p>\n<p>Please be careful, always check the code before upvoting, and let's not reward this kind of cheating behavior.</p>",
      "feedbackTrackingData": {},
      "id": 3440558,
      "isThankYou": false,
      "kernelVersion": 0,
      "parent": {},
      "postDate": "2026-04-12T16:01:29.320Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "I would like to bring the community's attention to a deceptive practice currently happening in the notebooks section to farm upvotes.\n\n[nvidianemotron 0.81 new making 0.85 public soon](https://www.kaggle.com/code/atahalam/nvidianemotron-0-81-new-making-0-85-public-soon)\n\n**Why this notebook is fake and deceptive:**\n1. **Output Copying (Plagiarism):** The code inside this notebook is completely fake and does not generate the score it claims through actual modeling. Instead, it simply copies the `submission.zip` or outputs from other hard-working Kagglers' top-performing public notebooks directly into `/kaggle/working/`. \n2. **Clickbait Titles:** The author intentionally uses misleading titles like *\"making 0.85 public soon\"* to deceive users and farm upvotes. Furthermore, they have a history of writing fabricated scores in the titles that are completely different from what the actual code inside achieves.\n3. **Disabled Comments:** To prevent anyone from pointing out these issues or warning others, the author has deliberately disabled the comments section on the notebook.\n\n**This behavior disrespects the hard work of original authors and clutters the platform with spam.**\n\nPlease be careful, always check the code before upvoting, and let's not reward this kind of cheating behavior.",
